      "content": "Even if your doctor didn't specify St. John's Wort, it's still best to consult a pharmacist or healthcare provider before adding any supplement to your routine. St. John's Wort can interact with warfarin in unpredictable ways, and its effects can be severe. If you're looking for natural mood help, consider talking to your doctor about alternative, pharmaceutically supervised options or therapy, which can be more effective and safer than unregulated supplements.",
      "source": "target",
